From a8b20d1289f0dbea4fdd1534e7c1acb8063f4e65 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 19:03:38 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] lane-298 GDN deferred commit + replay (opt-in
 LLAMA_GDN_REPLAY=1): replay op, Vulkan GDN_REPLAY bank pipeline, recurrent
 wiring

grep-10051756 BUILD read: replay of 4 tokens costs 0.231 ms, GDN snapshot slice 4.643 ms/verify on qwen4exp.
- ggml_gated_delta_net_replay(q,k,v,g,beta,state,log,ctl,K,deferred): replays ctl[0] logged accepted tokens from the
  per-layer k|v|g|beta log (half ctl[1]) before the window. Deferred (window fits the log): 2 slots {committed, final},
  window logged into the other half, no per-token snapshots. Wide: K age snapshots as before, no log.
- CPU reference (shared step lambda), Vulkan GDN_REPLAY variant of the GDN_BANK shader (committed write skipped when
  P == 0 and in place; rep_plant push field for the planted RED), backend op test replay cases.
- memory-recurrent: rep bookkeeping per cell, +1 ssm plane (committed never aliases final at n == K), read final on full
  accept and committed + replay after a rollback, rollback limited to the logged window, rep reset on state restore.
- graph inputs rep_ctl / rep_wrow (runtime contents, graph reuse kept); server: after a partial ring accept the next
  draft is capped to n_rs_seq so no checkpoint is taken of an unmaterialized state (Q19).
Replaces the GGML_VK_GDN_REPLAY_DIAG prologue.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit cf4f877c074c1c21121efcbfef04cadc9b0f5a89)

Origin: ArifiLabs (native) - fork-authored (lane-298); no upstream origin exists.
Measured-effect: UNMEASURED on its own - supporting commit; see release ledger Table 2 (lane 298), the number sits on that win's main commit
